  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing the level of vulnerability in relation to access to food, the protectio</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Over a 12 -month period, the project will be delivered in the departments of Fouli and Kaya, in particular the townships of Daboua, Liwa and Baga Sola with the aim of reducing the impact of multiple incidents on women, young girls, men and young boys through a multi -sector humanitarian response effort that focuses on Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), food security and protection. The project is aligned with the goals of the Humanitarian Response Plan (HRP) 2022 for Chad with reference HTCD22 -PRO; FSC; WSH -187148 -1.  The project will reach 53,200 people, including 11,278 women, 10,002 men, 16,918 girls and 15,002 boys across all intervention zones, equal to 13% of the population (401,511) affected by the crisis over this time.</narrative>
  </description>
